    "body": "﻿<!-- pr-reviewer: dabd67196c769249b7e480c1d89eb7164b8a00ed -->\r\nReview (independent, docs-only): clean.\r\n\r\n- The new `git worktree add --no-track -b issue/N-<slug> .claude/worktrees/issue-N origin/main` line is consistent with the Issue Law claim/branch steps and the \"Done on a branch\" cleanup wording. The path is relative to the repo root, which is where the command runs.\r\n- `origin/main:.gitignore` has `/.claude/*` with exceptions only for `/.claude/agents/` and `/.claude/skills/`, so `.claude/worktrees/` is ignored.\r\n- Non-blocking leftover, already acknowledged in the PR body: AGENTS.md line ~518 (the `/review-prs` section) still says `../cc-pr<N>-review`. Fine to leave for the other session, but it is the same stale-location pattern.\r\n",
